### =====================
### STEP 1: Get CSRF token first!
### Run this authenticated GET request - check the response cookies for XSRF-TOKEN
### Copy the token value and paste it in the @csrf variable below
### =====================
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4=
Accept: application/json

### =====================
### Set your CSRF token here after running the GET request above
### Copy from response cookies tab: XSRF-TOKEN=<value>
### =====================
@csrf = YOUR_TOKEN_HERE
### DO NOT COMMIT THIS CHANGE!!!!

### =====================
### Books
### =====================

### Get all books
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books
Accept: application/json

### Create a new book (requires authentication + CSRF)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4=
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{
  "title": "The Great Gatsby",
  "description": "A novel about the American Dream"
}

### Edit a book
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/books/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4=
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Updated Book Title",
  "description": "Updated description"
}

### Delete a book
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books/1
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4=
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

### =====================
### Authentication
### =====================

### Authenticate (check current user)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/authenticate
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4=

### Sign up new user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/signup
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{
  "username": "newuser",
  "password": "password123",
  "email": "newuser@example.com"
}
